Subject: [PATCH] toolkit: Linux session-bus names claim org.aequera, never org.mozilla

Why Firefox source must change:
  Every D-Bus name an Aequera Linux build owns or advertises is baked into
  Gecko/widget sources as org.mozilla.* literals and templates. No build
  option, branding directory, or preference redirects them: GetDBusAppName
  (xpcom/glue/XREAppData.cpp) only supplies the leaf (the lowercased ini
  Name, aequera), while the vendor prefix lives in the format strings.
  Left as-is, a running Aequera owns org.mozilla.aequera{,.profile} on the
  session bus and advertises an org.mozilla interface, violating
  docs/RESTRICTIONS.md (no org.mozilla.* service is claimed) and colliding
  conceptually with Firefox's own names.

What it changes (vendor prefix only; derivation unchanged):
  - widget/gtk/DBusService.cpp: bus template org.mozilla.%s ->
    org.aequera.%s (a running build owns org.aequera.aequera),
    object-path template /org/mozilla/%s -> /org/aequera/%s.
  - toolkit/components/remote/nsDBusRemoteServer.cpp: single-instance
    remote bus org.mozilla.<app>.<profile> -> org.aequera.<app>.<profile>
    (including the default fallback), the advertised introspection
    interface, the interface name incoming calls are matched against, and
    the /org/mozilla/<app>/Remote object path. Derivation from
    GetDBusAppName and the MOZ_DBUS_APP_NAME override keep working;
    -no-remote semantics unchanged. Two stale code comments now name the
    Aequera form (the remaining org.mozilla mention is a factual reference
    to Mozilla's own flatpak desktop path, not a claimed name).

Depends on: nothing. Touches unique literals; independent of other series.
Validation: aequera patch check (applies cleanly); Linux artifact/compiled
  build + run: bus names and interface visible via busctl/d-feet;
  single-instance handoff between two Aequera instances still works and
  never hands off to Firefox.
Upstream risk: low. String literals in stable desktop-integration code;
  conflicts only if Mozilla restructures D-Bus naming.

diff --git a/toolkit/components/remote/nsDBusRemoteServer.cpp b/toolkit/components/remote/nsDBusRemoteServer.cpp
index 226b2dc52874..d5a959cc4c8e 100644
--- a/toolkit/components/remote/nsDBusRemoteServer.cpp
+++ b/toolkit/components/remote/nsDBusRemoteServer.cpp
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@ static const char* introspect_template =
     "1.0//EN\"\n"
     "\"http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/dbus/1.0/introspect.dtd\">\n"
     "<node>\n"
-    " <interface name=\"org.mozilla.%s\">\n"
+    " <interface name=\"org.aequera.%s\">\n"
     "   <method name=\"OpenURL\">\n"
     "     <arg name=\"url\" direction=\"in\" type=\"ay\"/>\n"
     "   </method>\n"
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@ static const char* introspect_template =
 bool nsDBusRemoteServer::HandleOpenURL(const gchar* aInterfaceName,
                                        const gchar* aMethodName,
                                        Span<const gchar> aParam) {
-  nsPrintfCString ourInterfaceName("org.mozilla.%s", mAppName.get());
+  nsPrintfCString ourInterfaceName("org.aequera.%s", mAppName.get());
 
   if ((strcmp("OpenURL", aMethodName) != 0) ||
       (strcmp(ourInterfaceName.get(), aInterfaceName) != 0)) {
@@ -128,7 +128,7 @@ static const GDBusInterfaceVTable gInterfaceVTable = {
     HandleMethodCall, HandleGetProperty, HandleSetProperty};
 
 void nsDBusRemoteServer::OnBusAcquired(GDBusConnection* aConnection) {
-  mPathName = nsPrintfCString("/org/mozilla/%s/Remote", mAppName.get());
+  mPathName = nsPrintfCString("/org/aequera/%s/Remote", mAppName.get());
   if (!g_variant_is_object_path(mPathName.get())) {
     g_warning("nsDBusRemoteServer: object path is not valid");
     return;
@@ -187,7 +187,7 @@ nsresult nsDBusRemoteServer::Startup(const char* aAppName,
   // Don't even try to start without any profile name
   if (!aProfileName || aProfileName[0] == '\0') return NS_ERROR_INVALID_ARG;
 
-  // aAppName is remoting name which can be something like org.mozilla.appname
+  // aAppName is remoting name which can be something like org.aequera.appname
   // or so.
   // For DBus service we rather use general application DBus identifier
   // which is shared by all DBus services.
@@ -199,7 +199,7 @@ nsresult nsDBusRemoteServer::Startup(const char* aAppName,
 
   mozilla::XREAppData::SanitizeNameForDBus(profileName);
 
-  nsPrintfCString busName("org.mozilla.%s.%s", mAppName.get(),
+  nsPrintfCString busName("org.aequera.%s.%s", mAppName.get(),
                           profileName.get());
   if (busName.Length() > DBUS_MAXIMUM_NAME_LENGTH) {
     busName.Truncate(DBUS_MAXIMUM_NAME_LENGTH);
@@ -207,7 +207,7 @@ nsresult nsDBusRemoteServer::Startup(const char* aAppName,
 
   // We don't have a valid busName yet - try to create a default one.
   if (!g_dbus_is_name(busName.get())) {
-    busName = nsPrintfCString("org.mozilla.%s.%s", mAppName.get(), "default");
+    busName = nsPrintfCString("org.aequera.%s.%s", mAppName.get(), "default");
     if (!g_dbus_is_name(busName.get())) {
       // We failed completely to get a valid bus name - just quit.
       g_warning("nsDBusRemoteServer: couldn't get a valid bus name!");
diff --git a/widget/gtk/DBusService.cpp b/widget/gtk/DBusService.cpp
index a700307288f3..3e3d331ea276 100644
--- a/widget/gtk/DBusService.cpp
+++ b/widget/gtk/DBusService.cpp
@@ -36,8 +36,8 @@ void DBusService::Run() {
 // Mozilla has old GIO version in build roots
 #define G_BUS_NAME_OWNER_FLAGS_DO_NOT_QUEUE GBusNameOwnerFlags(1 << 2)
 
-#define DBUS_BUS_NAME_TEMPLATE "org.mozilla.%s"
-#define DBUS_OBJECT_PATH_TEMPLATE "/org/mozilla/%s"
+#define DBUS_BUS_NAME_TEMPLATE "org.aequera.%s"
+#define DBUS_OBJECT_PATH_TEMPLATE "/org/aequera/%s"
 
 static const char* GetDBusBusName() {
   static const char* name = []() {
@@ -285,7 +285,7 @@ bool DBusService::StartFreedesktopListener() {
   }
 
   mDBusID = g_bus_own_name(
-      // if org.mozilla.Firefox is taken it means we're already running
